    "['mpls traffic-eng tunnels', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols mpls traffic-engineering mpls-forwarding', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set protocols mpls traffic-engineering mpls-forwarding', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset protocols mpls traffic-engineering mpls-forwarding\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, the exact equivalent for enabling MPLS Traffic Engineering (TE) tunnels is typically configured under `protocols mpls` hierarchy. The command `set protocols mpls traffic-engineering mpls-forwarding` enables MPLS TE functionality, which is the Juniper equivalent of Cisco's `mpls traffic-eng tunnels` interface-level command. \\n\\nFor interface-specific TE configuration in Juniper, you would additionally need to configure `family mpls` under the interface and TE-specific parameters if needed.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols mpls traffic-engineering mpls-forwarding'}]]": 1,
