    "['ip unnumbered [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces lo0 unit 0 family inet address 1.1.1.1/32', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset interfaces lo0 unit 0 family inet address 1.1.1.1/32\\nset interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 family inet unnumbered-address lo0.0\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, the equivalent of Cisco's `ip unnumbered Loopback1` would be to configure the interface with an unnumbered address pointing to the loopback interface. However, there are a few important distinctions:\\n\\n1. Juniper uses `gr-` (generic routing) or `ip-` (IP-over-IP) interfaces for tunnels rather than `Tunnel` interfaces\\n2. The loopback interface in Juniper is typically `lo0` rather than `Loopback1`\\n3. The unnumbered configuration is applied per unit (logical interface) in Juniper\\n\\nThe exact interface name might vary based on your tunnel implementation in Juniper (could be `ip-0/0/0` or similar). The key concept is using `unnumbered-address` pointing to the loopback interface.\", 'trans_template': 'set interfaces lo0 unit 0 family inet address 1.1.1.1/32'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 family inet unnumbered-address lo0.0', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset interfaces lo0 unit 0 family inet address 1.1.1.1/32\\nset interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 family inet unnumbered-address lo0.0\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, the equivalent of Cisco's `ip unnumbered Loopback1` would be to configure the interface with an unnumbered address pointing to the loopback interface. However, there are a few important distinctions:\\n\\n1. Juniper uses `gr-` (generic routing) or `ip-` (IP-over-IP) interfaces for tunnels rather than `Tunnel` interfaces\\n2. The loopback interface in Juniper is typically `lo0` rather than `Loopback1`\\n3. The unnumbered configuration is applied per unit (logical interface) in Juniper\\n\\nThe exact interface name might vary based on your tunnel implementation in Juniper (could be `ip-0/0/0` or similar). The key concept is using `unnumbered-address` pointing to the loopback interface.\", 'trans_template': 'set interfaces gr-0/0/0 unit 0 family inet unnumbered-address lo0.0'}]]": 1,
